Ship both arms, and ship the attribution with them. One pure function, one render line:

```ts
// eqlwiki Game Mechanics § Working Legends Damage Bonus Formula (T5 prose),
// corroborated by 19 Itempage statsBlocks (T2) and one client window (M).
const TWO_HANDED = new Set(['2H Slashing','2H Blunt','2H Piercing'])
const MELEE = new Set([...TWO_HANDED,'1H Slashing','1H Blunt','Piercing','Hand to Hand'])
export function dmgBonus(skill: string, dmg: number, delay: number, level: number) {
  if (!MELEE.has(skill)) return null
  const hand = TWO_HANDED.has(skill) ? 1.1 : 0.8
  return Math.floor(hand * Math.max(level, dmg) * (Math.min(delay, 50) / 40) * (level / 100))
}
```

Inputs you already hold: `wp.skill`, the tier-upgraded damage `Gt()` already computes, `wp.dly`, and a level. For level, reuse your own rule rather than inventing one — `ht(item, ctx)` already returns `{best, via}`, and your character-page copy already says "an item's level requirement is checked against the class that qualifies you for it."

Where it applies: **main hand only.** In `Kt()` the weapon object is attached only when `position === 'PRIMARY'` or `'SECONDARY'`, so set `bonus` on `weapons.primary` and leave `weapons.secondary` alone (measured off-hand bonus is 0, M). Any Slot needs no change — it never populates `weapons`.

Where it renders: the Weapons card, as a third term — `74/70 dmg/dly · ratio 1.057 · Dmg Bon 50`. Add it to the set-diff too, because on a big two-hander the bonus is not constant across +0..+10: it climbs once damage passes level.

Badge it honestly and it still reads well: **"Tier 5 formula, Tier 2 corroboration"** — a formula published on eqlwiki's Game Mechanics page, which exactly reproduces 19 printed `Dmg Bon` figures on eqlwiki item pages and your own +10 Earthshaker window. Two caveats belong in the note, because the wiki states them itself: the exact rounding at low levels is unsettled (its own L32 and L48 24-delay rows are off by one under truncation), and the `max(Level, Damage)` branch has not been isolated in-game. Both are invisible at level 50 with sub-50 damage, which is nearly every row you ship.
